  "prefLabel": "Ed 902.04 Graduation rate",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ed 902.04 “Graduation rate” means “graduation rate” as defined in RSA 189:59,I(k), namely, the number of seniors who receive a diploma from a high school divided by the number of students enrolled in this program at such high school.\n\nSource. #8582, eff 3-15-06; ss by #10649, eff 7-26-14",
